@page "/"

<PageTitle>EOH 2026 - Contest Judging</PageTitle>

<div class="container mt-4">
    <div class="hero-section text-center p-5 mb-5 text-white shadow-lg" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(19, 41, 75, 0.9) 0%, rgba(30, 34, 41, 0.85) 100%), url('assets/eohheader.svg') no-repeat center; background-size: cover; background-position: center; border-radius: var(--eoh-radius); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05); min-height: 320px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center;">
        <h1 class="display-3 mb-3 text-white" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); font-weight: 300; letter-spacing: -0.05rem; text-transform: none;">Forging the Future</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4 text-white-50" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.35rem; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem auto;">Relative Judging System for Engineering Open House 2026</p>
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-center gap-3">
            <a href="setup" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg px-5 shadow-sm" style="background-color: var(--eoh-orange); border-color: var(--eoh-orange); border-radius: 30px;">Get Started</a>
            <a href="results" class="btn btn-outline-light btn-lg px-5" style="border-radius: 30px; border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); font-weight: 600;">View Leaderboard</a>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="row text-start g-4">
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100 border-0">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h5 class="card-title" style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); font-weight: 600;"><i class="bi bi-gear-wide-connected me-2"></i>1. Setup</h5>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">Create judging categories and drop in your exhibit list. Got a lot of teams? Use the bulk import feature to set up the bracket in seconds.</p>
                    <a href="setup" class="btn btn-link p-0 fw-bold" style="color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange);">Configure Projects &rarr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100 border-0">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h5 class="card-title" style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); font-weight: 600;"><i class="bi bi-cpu-fill me-2"></i>2. Judging</h5>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">Put exhibits head-to-head. The system tracks the match-ups and suggests which pairs need to be compared next to build a complete ranking.</p>
                    <a href="judging" class="btn btn-link p-0 fw-bold" style="color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange);">Start Comparisons &rarr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card h-100 border-0">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h5 class="card-title" style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); font-weight: 600;"><i class="bi bi-bar-chart-fill me-2"></i>3. Results</h5>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">Check out the live standings. As judges make their calls, the leaderboard updates automatically using either linear or percentile scoring.</p>
                    <a href="results" class="btn btn-link p-0 fw-bold" style="color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange);">Analyze Results &rarr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5 p-5 bg-light shadow-sm">
        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-lg-8">
                <h2 class="mb-3" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); font-weight: 600; text-transform: none;">Why Relative Judging?</h2>
                <p class="lead text-muted" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.25rem;">With hundreds of brilliant exhibits on display across campus, maintaining consistent scoring is a serious challenge.</p>
                <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--eoh-charcoal);">Instead of assigning arbitrary numbers on a rubric, relative judging asks a simpler question: <strong>"Is Project A more innovative than Project B?"</strong> By focusing entirely on these direct match-ups, we eliminate score inflation and ensure the fairest possible ranking for everyone involved.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center d-none d-lg-block">
                <i class="bi bi-diagram-3" style="font-size: 8rem; color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); opacity: 0.15;"></i>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .hero-section {
        border-bottom: 4px solid var(--eoh-orange);
    }
</style>
